{
    "map": {
        "band_index.descr": "The bands that will be exported for the layer. If no bands are specified, all the bands will be used in the output.",
        "band_index.dt.title1": "ID",
        "band_index.title": "Bands",
        "cell_size.descr": "The cell size of the output mosaic layer.",
        "cell_size.title": "Output Cell Size",
        "description": "Creates a  mosaic layer from a mosaic dataset or layer file. The layer that is created by the tool is temporary and will not persist after the session ends unless the layer is saved as a layer file or the map  is saved.",
        "in_mosaic_dataset.descr": "The path and name of the input mosaic dataset.",
        "in_mosaic_dataset.title": "Mosaic Dataset",
        "lock_rasterid.descr": "The Raster ID or raster name to which the service should be locked so that only the specified rasters are displayed. If left undefined, it will be similar to the system default. Multiple IDs can be defined as a semicolon-delimited list.",
        "lock_rasterid.title": "Lock Raster ID",
        "mosaic_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Choose the mosaic method. The mosaic method defines how the layer is created from different rasters in the mosaic dataset.</p><ul><li><span title=\"CLOSEST_TO_CENTER\">Closest to center</span>—Sorts rasters based on an order where rasters that have their center closest to the view center are placed on top.</li><li><span title=\"NORTH_WEST\">Northwest</span>—Sorts rasters based on an order where rasters that have their center closest to the northwest are placed on top.</li><li><span title=\"LOCK_RASTER\">Lock raster</span>—Enables a user to lock the display of single or multiple rasters, based on an ID or name. When you choose this option, you need to specify the Lock Raster ID.</li><li><span title=\"BY_ATTRIBUTE\">By attribute</span>—Sorts rasters based on an attribute field and its difference from the base value. When this option is chosen, the order field and order base value parameters also need to be set.</li><li><span title=\"CLOSEST_TO_NADIR\">Closest to nadir</span>—Sorts rasters based on an order where rasters that have their nadir position closest to the view center are placed on top. The nadir point can be different from the center point, especially in oblique imagery.</li><li><span title=\"CLOSEST_TO_VIEWPOINT\">Closest to view point</span>—Sorts rasters based on an order where the nadir position is closest to the user-defined viewpoint location and are placed on top.</li><li><span title=\"SEAMLINE\">Seamline</span>—Cuts the rasters using the predefined seamline shape for each raster using optional feathering along the seams. The ordering is predefined during seamline generation. The LAST mosaic operator is not valid with this mosaic method.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "mosaic_method.title": "Mosaic Method",
        "mosaic_operator.descr": "<xdoc><p>Choose the mosaic operator to use. When two or more rasters have the same sort priority, this parameter is used to further refine the sort order.</p><ul><li><span title=\"FIRST\">First</span>—The first raster in the list will be on top. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"LAST\">Last</span>—The last raster in the list will be on top.</li><li><span title=\"MIN\">Minimum</span>—The raster with the lowest value will be on top.</li><li><span title=\"MAX\">Maximum</span>—The raster with the highest value will be on top.</li><li><span title=\"MEAN\">Mean</span>—The average pixel value will be on top.</li><li><span title=\"BLEND\">Blend</span>—The output cell value will be a blend of values; this blend value relies on an algorithm that is weight based and dependent on the distance from the pixel to the edge within the overlapping area.</li><li><span title=\"SUM\">Sum</span>—The output cell value will be the aggregate of all overlapping cells.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.BLEND": "Blend",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.FIRST": "First",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.LAST": "Last",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.MAX": "Maximum",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.MEAN": "Mean",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.MIN": "Minimum",
        "mosaic_operator.domain.SUM": "Sum",
        "mosaic_operator.title": "Mosaic Operator",
        "order_base_value.descr": "The order base value. The images are sorted based on the difference between this value and the attribute value in the specified field.",
        "order_base_value.title": "Order Base Value",
        "order_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>Choose the order field. When the mosaic method is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">By attribute</span>, the default field to use when ordering rasters needs to be set. The list of fields is defined as those in the service table that are of type metadata.</p></xdoc>",
        "order_field.title": "Order Field",
        "out_mosaic_layer.descr": "The name of the output mosaic layer.",
        "out_mosaic_layer.title": "Output Mosaic Layer",
        "params.category1": "Mosaic Properties",
        "processing_template.descr": "<xdoc><p>The raster function processing template that can be applied on the output mosaic layer.</p><ul><li><span title=\"None\">None</span>—No processing template.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "processing_template.domain.None": "None",
        "processing_template.title": "Processing Template",
        "sort_order.descr": "<xdoc><p>Choose whether the sort order is ascending or descending.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ASCENDING\">Ascending</span>—The sort order will be ascending. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"DESCENDING\">Descending</span>—The sort order will be descending.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "sort_order.domain.ASCENDING": "Ascending",
        "sort_order.domain.DESCENDING": "Descending",
        "sort_order.title": "Sort Order",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Creates a mosaic layer from a mosaic dataset or layer file. The layer that is created by the tool is temporary and will not persist after the session ends unless the layer is saved as a layer file or the map is saved.</p><p>This tool can be used to make a layer so you can work with a specified subset of bands in a mosaic dataset.</p></xdoc>",
        "template.descr": "<xdoc><p>The output extent can be specified by defining the four coordinates or by using the extent of an existing layer.</p><ul><li>Current Display Extent—The extent will be based on the active map or scene.</li><li>Draw Extent—The extent will be based on a rectangle drawn on the map or scene.</li><li>Extent of a Layer—The extent will be based on an active map layer. Choose an available layer or use the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Extent of data in all layers</span> option. Each map layer has the following options:<p><ul><li>All Features—The extent of all features.</li><li>Selected Features —The extent of the selected features.</li><li>Visible Features—The extent of visible features.</li></ul></p></li><li>Browse—The extent will be based on a dataset.</li><li>Clipboard—The extent can be copied to and from the clipboard.<ul><li>Copy Extent—Copies the extent and coordinate system to the clipboard.</li><li>Paste Extent—Pastes the extent and coordinate system from the clipboard. If the clipboard does not include a coordinate system, the extent will use the map’s coordinate system.</li></ul></li><li>Reset Extent—The extent will be reset to the default value.</li></ul><p>When coordinates are manually provided, the coordinates must be numeric values and in the active map&apos;s coordinate system. The map may use different display units than the provided coordinates. Use a negative value sign for south and west coordinates.</p></xdoc>",
        "template.title": "Template Extent",
        "title": "Make Mosaic Layer",
        "where_clause.descr": "Define a query using SQL or use the Query Builder to build a query.",
        "where_clause.title": "Expression"
    }
}
